task: raft-prevote
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/raft-prevote
worktree: ../okay-wt-pv

why: the sweeps show a healed partition costing terms — a node cut
  off campaigns on its own, returns with a term nobody needs, and
  deposes a working leader whose log is ahead of its own; stage 2a
  answered the REMOVED server's version of this by silence, and the
  member's version is what the thesis's pre-vote (§4.2.3, §9.6) is
  for. Measured, not assumed: terms per seed in both sweeps before
  and after.

what: a PreVote round before a real election — the would-be
  candidate asks, at its NEXT term without adopting it, whether the
  others would vote for it; a voter grants only if it would (log up
  to date, term not behind) AND it has not heard from a leader within
  an election timeout, which the CALLER tells the core (the core has
  no clock): `Raft.handle(s, msg, peers, leaderFresh)`. A majority of
  pre-votes starts the election as before; less, and the node waits
  for its next timeout with its term untouched. RaftRole gains
  PreCandidate. The wire tracks when it last heard a leader.
